## Backend Framework & APIs

### 1. Express.js Fundamentals

**Express.js Explanation:**
Express.js is a minimal and flexible Node.js web application framework. It provides a thin layer of fundamental features without obscuring Node.js features, making it perfect for building APIs and web applications.

**Key Features:**
- Routing - Map HTTP methods and paths to handlers
- Middleware - Chainable functions that process requests/responses
- Simple API - Minimal boilerplate, easy to learn
- Flexible - Works for simple APIs to complex applications

```javascript
const express = require('express');
const app = express();

// Built-in middleware - parse JSON request bodies
app.use(express.json());

// Serve static files from public directory
app.use(express.static('public'));

// Custom middleware - executes for all requests
app.use((req, res, next) => {
  console.log(`${req.method} ${req.path}`); // Log request
  next(); // Pass to next middleware
});

// GET route - retrieve data
app.get('/users', (req, res) => {
  res.json({ users: [] }); // Send JSON response
});

// POST route - create data
app.post('/users', (req, res) => {
  const user = req.body; // Request body is parsed JSON
  res.status(201).json(user); // 201 = Created
});

// PUT route - update data
app.put('/users/:id', (req, res) => {
  const { id } = req.params; // Extract path parameter
  res.json({ id, ...req.body });
});

// DELETE route - remove data
app.delete('/users/:id', (req, res) => {
  res.sendStatus(204); // 204 = No Content
});

// Error handling middleware - 4 parameters (err, req, res, next)
// Must come AFTER all other middlewares
app.use((err, req, res, next) => {
  console.error(err.stack); // Log error
  res.status(500).json({ error: 'Internal Server Error' });
});

// Start server
app.listen(3000, () => {
  console.log('Server running on port 3000');
});
```

**Theory Notes:**
- Middleware runs in order defined
- `next()` passes control to next middleware
- Error middleware requires 4 parameters (Express recognizes by arity)
- Status codes: 2xx (success), 3xx (redirect), 4xx (client error), 5xx (server error)
- HTTP methods: GET (read), POST (create), PUT (update), DELETE (remove)

### 2. Routing & Middleware Architecture

```javascript
