**Q11: Explain memory leaks and how to detect them.**

A: Memory leaks occur when memory is allocated but never freed, gradually consuming more RAM.

**Common causes:**
- Unbounded cache
- Circular references
- Event listeners never removed
- Timers never cleared

```javascript
// MEMORY LEAK: Cache grows indefinitely
const cache = {};
app.get('/user/:id', async (req, res) => {
  cache[req.params.id] = await getUser(req.params.id);
  res.json(cache[req.params.id]);
});

// FIX: Use size-limited cache with TTL
const LRU = require('lru-cache');
const cache = new LRU({ max: 1000, maxAge: 3600000 });

// Detect leaks
setInterval(() => {
  const memUsage = process.memoryUsage();
  console.log(`Heap: ${Math.round(memUsage.heapUsed / 1024 / 1024)}MB`);
}, 5000);

// Use tools like: clinic.js, 0x profiler
```

